CASE SOURCE — no steps in AWPTCM or ck.db (queue issue I-2)
================================================================================
No ck.db case was mapped onto this one. Graded against:
1. TPS — wiki "X960_platform_support_TPS" row 26, group "DHCP server": **Option 82,
   priority 1, Yes.**
   ⚠ **The TPS groups Option 82 under "DHCP server", but it is NOT a server feature.** The
   governing TFS says so explicitly: "DHCP Relay and DHCP Snooping behavior will be affected by
   this project. DHCP Client and DHCP Server will not be affected." This case therefore tests
   the DUT as a RELAY, which is why triage re-cut it out of the server group and into group B
   beside T43852. The TPS row name is a grouping artefact, not a statement about the feature.
2. Functional spec — wiki "DHCP Option 82 Remote ID TFS", requirements S1566.100.01 … .15.
3. DHCP Feature Overview and Configuration Guide (C613-22102-00 REV G), "Configuring DHCP relay
   agent information option (Option 82)", pp20-22.
4. AW+ CLI pages: `ip-dhcp-relay-agent-option`, `-remote-id`, `-checking`,
   `ip-dhcp-relay-information-policy`.

Key graded requirements, verbatim:
  S1566.100.01 "Include the remote-id in the option-82 field if option-82 is being inserted by
               the DHCP relay service. The switch MAC address will be used by default"
  S1566.100.02 "Provide the ability to configure content of the remote-id field inserted by
               DHCP relay"
  S1566.100.06 "The circuit Id for DHCP Relay can not be configured ... it will remain at the
               ISC default which is inserting a string which describes the VLAN interface,
               i.e. vlan2"
  S1566.100.07 CLI "ip dhcp-relay agent-option remote-id ascii_string" ... "it will only be
               allow when the agent-option command is enabled"
  S1566.100.08 CLI "no ip dhcp-relay agent-option remote-id". The switch MAC address with be
               inserted by default

