dhcp4.py gained, during this case, two generic things, both in its README entry:
  --option82-override on the server, to return a MISMATCHED option 82 and so exercise relay
  response-path checking; and reporting of DUPLICATE option 82 fields (see STEP 6).

🔴 The scapy option-82 trap recorded in T43851 paid off exactly here: option 82 must be built
as `("relay_agent_information", raw)`. The integer key 82 serialises a frame with no option at
all and raises nothing, which in this case would have read as "the relay did not insert
option 82" and graded a working device defective.

