================================================================================
METHOD — STANDING-ORDERS §7 (scapy, not ping)
================================================================================
Every leg sends 3 distinct crafted DHCPDISCOVERs from eth3 and reads option 82 out of the
frames, three ways: tcpdump on eth4 (how many the DUT relayed), the scapy server's per-frame
record on eth4 (what option 82 the DUT INSERTED, decoded sub-option by sub-option), and the
client's own received OFFER on eth3 (what option 82, if any, came BACK). Every positive leg is
paired with a leg in the same configuration that must not produce it. Nothing rests on
`show ip dhcp-relay`; the show output is corroboration read after the frames.

================================================================================
STEP 1 — BASELINE OFF: no option 82 is inserted when insertion is disabled
================================================================================
Insertion is disabled by default, so this control costs nothing and comes first.

  leg `baseline-off`, 3 clients, no option 82 sent by the client
  COUNTED: 6 frames relayed on eth4 (3 DISCOVER + 3 REQUEST), offers 3/3, acks 3/3
  SERVER side — every relayed DISCOVER:
      chaddr=02:e8:00:00:10:01 giaddr=192.168.10.1  option82: ABSENT
      chaddr=02:e8:00:00:10:02 giaddr=192.168.10.1  option82: ABSENT
      chaddr=02:e8:00:00:10:03 giaddr=192.168.10.1  option82: ABSENT

Relaying works perfectly and carries NO option 82. STEP 1 PASS — and this is the control that
every later leg's insertion is measured against.

================================================================================
