================================================================================
Run while insertion was still disabled, before enabling it:

  awplus(config-if)# ip dhcp-relay agent-option remote-id CK-REMOTE-82
  % Can not configure DHCP Relay agent option remote-id unless agent option is set

Refused with a specific, accurate message, exactly as S1566.100.07 requires. STEP 2 PASS.

================================================================================
STEP 3 — INSERTION ON: circuit-id is `vlan10`, remote-id is the switch MAC
================================================================================
  awplus(config-if)# ip dhcp-relay agent-option      (cfg.py exit 0, no "% " lines)
  show ip dhcp-relay -> Insertion of Relay Agent Option is enabled

  leg `agent-option-on`, 3 clients. COUNTED: 6 relayed, offers 3/3, acks 3/3.
  SERVER side — option 82 as the DUT built it, identical on all three:
      raw = 0106 766c616e3130 0208 0006e01aead47043
      sub-option 1 (circuit-id), len 6  = "vlan10"
      sub-option 2 (remote-id),  len 8  = 00 06 e0 1a ea d4 70 43

  - **circuit-id = `vlan10`** — the ISC default string naming the client-side VLAN interface,
    exactly as S1566.100.06 says, and it is not configurable (no CLI exists for it).
  - **remote-id = the switch MAC** e0:1a:ea:d4:70:43, per S1566.100.01, carried with a 2-byte
    inner type/length prefix `00 06` (type 0 = binary, length 6). It matches what
    `show ip dhcp-relay` reports as "The Remote Id string ... is e01a.ead4.7043".
STEP 3 PASS. Paired against STEP 1 (same bench, same crafted flow, option 82 absent), this is
the matched pair for insertion.

