VERDICT: PASS -- the relay's Option 82 handling is correct on every graded limb. With insertion
disabled no option 82 is added; enabled, it inserts circuit-id "vlan10" (the ISC default, not
configurable per S1566.100.06) and remote-id = the switch MAC (S1566.100.01). The remote-id is
configurable to an ASCII string and reverts to the MAC on its no-form, proven on the wire
(S1566.100.02/.08), and is correctly refused while agent-option is disabled (S1566.100.07). All
four `information policy` actions behave as documented -- replace, keep, append (two TLVs,
client's then the relay's) and drop (zero relayed). `agent-option checking` validates option 82
in SERVER RESPONSES, dropping all 3 replies carrying mismatched information and passing all 3
that matched. Option 82 is stripped from every reply delivered to the client per RFC 3046, and
all settings survive a reboot.
